# Frontend's own config. Copy to .env for local dev:
#   cp .env.example .env
# .env is gitignored; never commit real values. Vite only exposes
# variables prefixed VITE_ to client code (see src/lib/env.ts).

# Base URL of rust_gateway (see ../rust_gateway/.env.example's
# GATEWAY_HOST/GATEWAY_PORT — must match whatever that process actually
# binds to). No trailing slash. Workspaces AND per-workspace onboarding
# (`/workspaces/:id/onboarding/*`) both go through this origin — never
# call the wrapper's own listen address from the browser.
#
# MUST use the SAME HOSTNAME SPELLING as this dev server's own origin
# (compare against ../rust_gateway/.env's FRONTEND_ORIGIN, which this
# frontend is served from — normally "localhost", see vite's own default
# bind). "localhost" and "127.0.0.1" resolve to the same machine but are
# DIFFERENT SITES for cookies (see rust_gateway/src/auth/route.rs's
# SameSite=Strict session cookie): a mismatch here means login appears to
# succeed (the Set-Cookie is received) but every following request 401s,
# because the browser silently refuses to send a SameSite=Strict cookie
# across a "localhost" vs "127.0.0.1" boundary — confirmed live, not
# hypothetical; this is a real, non-obvious footgun CORS alone did not
# have (CORS's own allow-list already tolerates either spelling, cookies
# do not). Keep both this value and FRONTEND_ORIGIN on the SAME spelling.
VITE_GATEWAY_URL=http://localhost:8080
